WEBVTT

00:04:34.809 --> 00:04:36.039
Storm's coming.

00:04:36.039 --> 00:04:38.949
And you boys, you are
smack in the middle of it.

00:04:40.459 --> 00:04:44.669
Dad wants us to pick up where he left
off... saving people, hunting things.

00:04:46.659 --> 00:04:47.649
Family business.

00:04:47.649 --> 00:04:49.649
I'm gonna save as many people as we can.

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:54.329
Dean, you and I have seen things
most people couldn't even dream about.

00:04:57.119 --> 00:04:58.349
If it's supernatural, we kill it.

00:04:58.349 --> 00:04:59.439
End of story. That's our job.

00:04:59.439 --> 00:05:00.889
No, Dean, that is not our job.

00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:02.289
Our job is hunting evil.

00:05:02.289 --> 00:05:03.749
They're all the same, Sam.

00:05:03.749 --> 00:05:05.289
They're not human, okay?

00:05:05.289 --> 00:05:07.159
We have to exterminate
every last one of them.

00:05:07.159 --> 00:05:08.879
Our lives are weird, man.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.839
You're telling me.

00:05:32.769 --> 00:05:34.189
We're lost.

00:05:34.189 --> 00:05:34.799
No.

00:05:34.799 --> 00:05:36.179
This is a short cut...

00:05:37.159 --> 00:05:41.289
Babe, it's just we've been on this road over
an hour, and we haven't seen a single car.

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:43.669
Molly, I know how to
read a frickin' map, okay?

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:46.589
We passed a gas station a while back.

00:05:46.589 --> 00:05:47.509
Let's just go ask someone.

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:48.369
That was 40 minutes ago.

00:05:48.369 --> 00:05:49.509
We're not turning around.

00:05:49.509 --> 00:05:51.159
Come on.

00:05:51.159 --> 00:05:53.889
Isn't this argument a little archaic?

00:05:54.609 --> 00:05:56.399
Men can ask directions these days.

00:05:56.399 --> 00:05:57.219
No, we can't.

00:05:57.219 --> 00:05:58.459
It's against our genetic code.

00:05:58.459 --> 00:06:00.359
Look, I know exactly where we are.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:01.919
Oh, yeah? Where?

00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:03.809
Highway 99, okay?

00:06:03.809 --> 00:06:05.408
It cuts right through.

00:06:09.739 --> 00:06:11.539
Highway 99, huh?

00:06:15.669 --> 00:06:19.239
Okay, so we're taking the scenic route.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:20.909
David.

00:06:21.429 --> 00:06:24.319
It's our anniversary, and we're
spending it stuck in the car.

00:06:24.799 --> 00:06:25.399
I know.

00:06:25.399 --> 00:06:26.659
I'm sorry.

00:06:28.189 --> 00:06:30.099
Let me make it up to
you, okay? Come here.

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:32.389
Stop. I'm mad at you.

00:06:32.709 --> 00:06:34.209
Oh, come on, Molly.

00:06:34.209 --> 00:06:36.639
Hey, you love me.

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:37.879
No, I don't.

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:39.499
You're a jerk.

00:06:41.859 --> 00:06:43.519
David, I mean it.

00:06:43.629 --> 00:06:44.579
Molly!

00:07:21.609 --> 00:07:22.829
David?

00:07:27.839 --> 00:07:29.069
David?

00:07:33.729 --> 00:07:34.919
David?

00:07:49.019 --> 00:07:50.399
David?

00:07:56.429 --> 00:07:58.278
Da... David?!

00:08:08.109 --> 00:08:09.539
David?!

00:08:15.019 --> 00:08:16.339
David?

00:08:42.089 --> 00:08:43.159
Hello?

00:08:44.859 --> 00:08:46.259
Is anyone here?

00:08:49.179 --> 00:08:50.609
Hello?

00:09:09.078 --> 00:09:10.288
It's you.

00:09:11.028 --> 00:09:11.759
You're okay.

00:09:12.058 --> 00:09:12.949
I'm so sorry.

00:09:12.949 --> 00:09:14.359
I didn't see you there.

00:09:15.219 --> 00:09:15.969
Are you...

00:09:16.729 --> 00:09:17.699
Are you hurt?

00:09:19.278 --> 00:09:20.339
Sir?

00:09:59.639 --> 00:10:02.578
Stop!

00:10:09.369 --> 00:10:10.778
You've got to help me.

00:10:12.838 --> 00:10:13.609
Please.

00:10:13.609 --> 00:10:14.578
Please!

00:10:14.578 --> 00:10:15.229
All right, all right.

00:10:15.229 --> 00:10:16.679
Calm down, calm down.

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:17.919
Tell us what happened.

00:10:17.919 --> 00:10:20.318
I-I swerved,
a-And we crashed.

00:10:20.318 --> 00:10:25.489
And when I came to, the car was
wrecked and my husband was missing.

00:10:26.609 --> 00:10:30.489
I went looking for him, but that's when the
man from the road, he... he started chasing me.

00:10:31.109 --> 00:10:34.599
Did he look like he lost
a fight with a lawn mower?

00:10:35.249 --> 00:10:36.659
How did you know that?

00:10:38.019 --> 00:10:39.189
Lucky guess.

00:10:40.349 --> 00:10:42.499
Ma'am, what's your name?

00:10:42.499 --> 00:10:43.609
Molly.

00:10:43.939 --> 00:10:45.429
Molly Mcnamara.

00:10:45.429 --> 00:10:47.589
I think maybe you should come with us.

00:10:47.589 --> 00:10:48.509
We'll take you back into town.

00:10:48.509 --> 00:10:49.709
I can't.

00:10:49.709 --> 00:10:50.859
I have to find David.

00:10:50.859 --> 00:10:52.219
He might have gone back to the car.

00:10:52.219 --> 00:10:53.838
We should get you somewhere safe first.

00:10:53.838 --> 00:10:55.259
Then Dean and I will come back.

00:10:55.259 --> 00:10:56.199
We'll look for your husband.

00:10:56.199 --> 00:10:56.659
No.

00:10:56.659 --> 00:10:58.818
I'm not leaving here without him.

00:11:02.229 --> 00:11:05.298
Would you just take me
back to my car, please?

00:11:07.838 --> 00:11:08.619
Of course.

00:11:08.669 --> 00:11:09.959
Come on.

00:11:30.788 --> 00:11:32.038
It's right over there.

00:11:37.818 --> 00:11:39.249
I don't understand.

00:11:40.019 --> 00:11:41.489
I'm sure this is where it was.

00:11:41.489 --> 00:11:43.409
W-We hit that tree right there.

00:11:44.318 --> 00:11:46.568
This... this doesn't make any sense.

00:11:50.359 --> 00:11:51.609
Dean, we got to get out of here.

00:11:51.838 --> 00:11:53.249
Greeley could show up at any second.

00:11:53.249 --> 00:11:54.058
What are you gonna tell her.

00:11:55.298 --> 00:11:56.159
The truth?

00:11:56.949 --> 00:11:59.058
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:11:59.479 --> 00:12:02.548
I know it sounds crazy, but
I crashed into that tree.

00:12:02.619 --> 00:12:03.929
I don't know who could've taken it.

00:12:03.929 --> 00:12:05.629
It was totaled.

00:12:07.949 --> 00:12:09.649
Please. You have to believe me.

00:12:10.699 --> 00:12:12.818
Molly, listen, we do believe you.

00:12:12.818 --> 00:12:14.949
But that's why we want
to get you out of here.

00:12:14.949 --> 00:12:16.669
What about David?

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:17.879
Something must have happened.

00:12:17.879 --> 00:12:19.119
I have to get to the cops.

00:12:19.119 --> 00:12:20.578
Cops... that's a great idea.

00:12:20.578 --> 00:12:22.349
We'll take you down to
the station ourselves.

00:12:22.349 --> 00:12:24.558
So just come with us.

00:12:24.558 --> 00:12:27.119
It's the best way we can
help you and your husband.

00:12:30.969 --> 00:12:32.239
Okay.

00:12:41.269 --> 00:12:43.629
We're supposed to be in lake Tahoe.

00:12:44.099 --> 00:12:45.359
You and David?

00:12:45.889 --> 00:12:47.689
It's our five-Year anniversary.

00:12:48.239 --> 00:12:50.009
Hell of an anniversary.

00:12:51.369 --> 00:12:54.389
Right before, we were
having the dumbest fight.

00:12:56.219 --> 00:12:59.009
It was the only time we ever really
argued... when we were stuck in the car.

00:12:59.009 --> 00:13:00.269
Yeah.

00:13:00.548 --> 00:13:02.239
I know how that goes.

00:13:03.869 --> 00:13:05.808
You know the last thing I said to him?

00:13:07.578 --> 00:13:09.068
I called him a jerk.

00:13:10.179 --> 00:13:11.058
Oh, god.

00:13:13.209 --> 00:13:15.509
What if that's the last
thing I said to him?

00:13:16.798 --> 00:13:17.669
Molly...

00:13:18.639 --> 00:13:20.558
We're gonna figure out what
happened to your husband.

00:13:20.848 --> 00:13:22.048
I promise.

00:13:29.619 --> 00:13:31.949
Did you? No.

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.869
I was afraid you'd say that.

00:13:38.699 --> 00:13:39.979
This song.

00:13:40.788 --> 00:13:41.629
What?

00:13:42.209 --> 00:13:44.828
It was playing when we crashed.

00:13:50.578 --> 00:13:51.939
She's mine.

00:13:52.798 --> 00:13:54.669
She's mine.

00:13:55.379 --> 00:13:56.389
She's mine.

00:13:56.389 --> 00:13:57.959
What is that?

00:14:02.649 --> 00:14:03.818
Hold on.

00:14:04.278 --> 00:14:05.989
What are you doing?

00:14:14.659 --> 00:14:15.548
What the...

00:14:17.058 --> 00:14:18.409
What the hell just happened?

00:14:18.409 --> 00:14:18.999
Don't worry, Molly.

00:14:18.999 --> 00:14:20.548
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:14:23.719 --> 00:14:25.798
Spoke a little too soon, Sammy.

00:14:46.739 --> 00:14:48.179
I don't think he's gonna let her leave.

00:14:58.239 --> 00:14:59.568
This can't be happening.

00:15:00.048 --> 00:15:00.778
Well...

00:15:01.828 --> 00:15:03.939
Trust me, it's happening.

00:15:15.979 --> 00:15:17.108
Well...

00:15:17.269 --> 00:15:18.328
Okay.

00:15:18.568 --> 00:15:21.298
Thanks for helping, but I think
I got it covered from here.

00:15:21.749 --> 00:15:22.259
Wait.

00:15:22.259 --> 00:15:23.159
Molly, Molly, wait a minute.

00:15:23.159 --> 00:15:24.209
Just leave me alone.

00:15:24.209 --> 00:15:25.409
No. Please. You have to listen to me.

00:15:25.409 --> 00:15:26.469
Just stay away.

00:15:26.828 --> 00:15:28.929
It wasn't a coincidence
that we found you, all right?

00:15:30.459 --> 00:15:31.619
What are you talking about?

00:15:31.729 --> 00:15:33.769
We weren't cruising for chicks
when we ran into you, sister.

00:15:33.769 --> 00:15:35.009
We were already out here.

00:15:35.288 --> 00:15:36.179
Hunting.

00:15:36.179 --> 00:15:38.088
Hunting for what?

00:15:40.048 --> 00:15:41.019
Ghosts.

00:15:42.778 --> 00:15:45.278
D... d... don't...

00:15:45.548 --> 00:15:47.189
Sugar coat it for her.

00:15:47.189 --> 00:15:48.489
You're nuts.

00:15:48.649 --> 00:15:49.649
Really?

00:15:49.719 --> 00:15:52.939
About as nuts as a vanishing
guy with his guts spilling out.

00:15:55.619 --> 00:15:56.808
You know what you saw.

00:16:05.219 --> 00:16:07.108
We think his name is Jonah Greeley.

00:16:08.369 --> 00:16:12.869
He was a local farmer that died
15 years ago on this highway.

00:16:12.959 --> 00:16:15.149
Just stop.

00:16:15.149 --> 00:16:19.889
One night a year, on the anniversary
of his death, he haunts this road.

00:16:21.139 --> 00:16:22.578
That's why we're here, Molly.

00:16:23.689 --> 00:16:24.919
To try and stop him.

00:16:25.949 --> 00:16:30.659
Now, I suppose this ghost
made my car disappear, too.

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:32.229
Crazier things have happened.

00:16:32.229 --> 00:16:33.269
Huh?

00:16:34.068 --> 00:16:34.999
You know what?

00:16:35.429 --> 00:16:37.338
I'm all filled up on crazy.

00:16:37.338 --> 00:16:39.239
I'm gonna get the cops myself.

00:16:39.239 --> 00:16:41.769
I don't mean to be harsh, but I
don't think you're gonna get too far.

00:16:42.689 --> 00:16:44.058
What is that supposed to mean?

00:16:44.058 --> 00:16:46.318
Means that plan "a" was
trying to get you out of here.

00:16:46.318 --> 00:16:49.899
Obviously that didn't go over too
well with, uh, farmer road kill.

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:55.308
Molly, we're telling the truth.

00:16:57.098 --> 00:16:59.298
Greeley's not gonna let
you leave this highway.

00:17:00.409 --> 00:17:05.689
You're s... you're serious
about this, aren't you?

00:17:06.209 --> 00:17:07.548
Deadly.

00:17:11.379 --> 00:17:14.798
Everyear, Greeley finds someone
to punish for what happened to him.

00:17:17.129 --> 00:17:18.699
Tonight that person is you.

00:17:18.869 --> 00:17:19.499
Why me?

00:17:19.499 --> 00:17:21.219
I didn't do anything.

00:17:21.219 --> 00:17:22.469
Doesn't matter.

00:17:24.179 --> 00:17:26.019
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:17:29.729 --> 00:17:33.989
So you're saying this
Greeley, he took my husband?

00:17:36.808 --> 00:17:37.899
Oh, god.

00:17:39.189 --> 00:17:41.239
Molly, look, we're
gonna help, all right?

00:17:43.469 --> 00:17:45.119
But first, you got to help us.

00:17:46.369 --> 00:17:47.528
Help you?

00:17:50.048 --> 00:17:51.098
How?

00:17:54.769 --> 00:17:55.338
This is it.

00:17:55.338 --> 00:17:56.818
This is where I saw him.

00:18:01.298 --> 00:18:02.679
Must have been his hunting cabin.

00:18:09.328 --> 00:18:10.869
Seemed like a real sweet guy.

00:18:14.969 --> 00:18:16.788
No markers or headstones outside.

00:18:16.969 --> 00:18:18.439
You're looking for Greeley's grave?

00:18:18.439 --> 00:18:19.409
Yeah.

00:18:19.679 --> 00:18:20.578
Why?

00:18:20.669 --> 00:18:22.949
So we can dig up the
corpse and salt and burn it.

00:18:23.778 --> 00:18:24.699
Oh.

00:18:25.058 --> 00:18:26.568
Sure. Naturally.

00:18:26.568 --> 00:18:28.419
It's a way to get rid of a spirit.

00:18:28.939 --> 00:18:30.348
And that'll save David?

00:18:30.348 --> 00:18:33.848
This is what'll help both of you,
provided there's a corpse to be found.

00:18:35.019 --> 00:18:36.129
So how do we find it?

00:18:36.129 --> 00:18:37.169
Uh, not sure.

00:18:37.169 --> 00:18:39.318
After Greeley died, his
wife claimed the body.

00:18:39.318 --> 00:18:41.088
And that was the last anyone saw of her.

00:18:41.088 --> 00:18:42.499
So good guess she brought him back here.

00:18:42.499 --> 00:18:44.308
But they have a thousand acres.

00:18:44.308 --> 00:18:46.338
He could be buried anywhere on 'em.

00:18:46.519 --> 00:18:48.088
Is is really what you guys do.

00:18:48.088 --> 00:18:49.608
You're like ghost busters.

00:18:49.608 --> 00:18:50.159
Yeah.

00:18:50.159 --> 00:18:51.239
Minus the jumpsuits.

00:18:51.239 --> 00:18:53.269
This is a fascinating
conversation and all.

00:18:53.269 --> 00:18:56.568
But this highway is only haunted once a year,
and we got till sun up to wrap this thing up.

00:18:56.568 --> 00:18:58.308
What do you say we move it along, okay?

00:18:58.308 --> 00:18:59.939
Great.

00:19:10.669 --> 00:19:12.098
What are we looking for?

00:19:12.098 --> 00:19:13.469
Greeley's house.

00:19:13.548 --> 00:19:15.058
Maybe he's buried there.

00:19:15.169 --> 00:19:16.909
Look for roads or paths or something.

00:19:16.909 --> 00:19:17.959
Stay close.

00:19:17.959 --> 00:19:18.439
Yeah.

00:19:18.439 --> 00:19:19.808
Okay.

00:19:26.528 --> 00:19:27.749
Molly?

00:19:29.189 --> 00:19:30.619
Molly, help me.

00:19:31.619 --> 00:19:32.869
Molly?

00:19:37.088 --> 00:19:39.519
David? David?

00:19:46.399 --> 00:19:48.009
Whoops.

00:19:54.009 --> 00:19:54.788
Hey!

00:19:54.788 --> 00:19:55.739
Are you all right?

00:19:55.739 --> 00:19:57.538
What has that son of a
bit chdone with my husband?

00:19:57.538 --> 00:20:00.149
Just take it easy, all right?

00:20:00.149 --> 00:20:01.479
You're gonna see David again.

00:20:01.479 --> 00:20:02.269
You will.

00:20:02.269 --> 00:20:03.489
Hey.

00:20:04.759 --> 00:20:06.389
Follow the creepy brick road.

00:20:08.189 --> 00:20:10.038
Go ahead.

00:20:22.509 --> 00:20:24.288
That thing shoots rock salt?

00:20:24.879 --> 00:20:25.729
Yep.

00:20:26.038 --> 00:20:28.308
And plain salt keeps away spirits?

00:20:29.159 --> 00:20:30.899
Simple remedies are always the best.

00:20:31.338 --> 00:20:36.139
In most cultures, salt is a symbol of purity,
so it repels impure and unnatural things.

00:20:36.139 --> 00:20:38.318
Same reason you throw
it over your shoulder.

00:20:43.659 --> 00:20:46.619
You know, just once I'd like to
round the corner and see a nice house.

00:21:22.189 --> 00:21:23.409
Any headstones outside?

00:21:23.409 --> 00:21:24.209
Yeah, right.

00:21:24.209 --> 00:21:25.589
Is it ever that easy?

00:21:25.589 --> 00:21:27.339
I guess not.

00:21:37.559 --> 00:21:38.609
You two check upstairs.

00:21:38.609 --> 00:21:41.009
See if you can find any notes or
records telling us where he's buried.

00:21:41.009 --> 00:21:42.288
I'll just check down here.

00:22:10.048 --> 00:22:11.099
Great.

00:22:35.749 --> 00:22:36.689
Look at this.

00:22:41.699 --> 00:22:43.538
It's Greeley and his wife.

00:23:03.629 --> 00:23:05.269
It's a love letter he wrote her.

00:23:07.229 --> 00:23:08.939
My god, it's beautiful.

00:23:13.159 --> 00:23:17.288
I don't understand how a guy like
this can turn into that monster.

00:23:21.589 --> 00:23:23.729
Spirits like Greeley are,uh...

00:23:25.069 --> 00:23:26.569
Like wounded animals.

00:23:27.759 --> 00:23:28.909
Lost.

00:23:30.139 --> 00:23:33.189
In so much pain, that they lash out.

00:23:33.849 --> 00:23:34.239
Why?

00:23:34.239 --> 00:23:35.519
Why are they here?

00:23:36.028 --> 00:23:37.999
Well, there's some part of them that...

00:23:38.919 --> 00:23:40.309
That's keeping them here.

00:23:41.639 --> 00:23:43.849
Like their remains or, um...

00:23:46.449 --> 00:23:47.709
Unfinished business.

00:23:48.409 --> 00:23:49.839
Unfinished business?

00:23:51.399 --> 00:23:52.129
Yeah.

00:23:54.169 --> 00:23:55.278
It could be revenge.

00:23:55.429 --> 00:23:57.209
Could be love.

00:23:57.889 --> 00:23:58.589
Or hate.

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:03.059
Whatever it is, they
just hold on too tight.

00:24:04.509 --> 00:24:05.889
Can't let go.

00:24:06.629 --> 00:24:07.599
So they're trapped.

00:24:09.769 --> 00:24:11.419
Caught in the same loops.

00:24:13.199 --> 00:24:15.879
Replaying the same
tragedies over and over.

00:24:16.359 --> 00:24:18.189
You sound almost sorry for them.

00:24:18.489 --> 00:24:20.829
Well, they weren't
evil people, you know?

00:24:21.999 --> 00:24:23.069
A lot of them were good.

00:24:23.089 --> 00:24:24.449
Just...

00:24:25.719 --> 00:24:26.919
Something happened to them.

00:24:28.259 --> 00:24:30.048
Something they couldn't control.

00:24:31.729 --> 00:24:35.079
Sammy's always getting a little J. Love
Hewitt when it comes to things like this.

00:24:37.249 --> 00:24:39.369
Me, I don't like 'em.

00:24:39.599 --> 00:24:41.619
And I sure as hell ain't
making apologies for 'em.

00:24:45.069 --> 00:24:46.079
There's nothing downstairs.

00:24:48.429 --> 00:24:51.749
Uh, just about every piece of
mail or receipt they ever had.

00:24:52.659 --> 00:24:55.189
Looked through a couple, but
nothing about a grave so far.

00:24:59.429 --> 00:25:00.298
What?

00:25:00.429 --> 00:25:01.778
There's something behind here.

00:25:02.778 --> 00:25:03.669
Here.

00:25:19.278 --> 00:25:20.809
It's locked from the inside.

00:25:45.999 --> 00:25:47.619
Smells like old lady in here.

00:25:56.829 --> 00:25:58.089
And that would explain why.

00:26:04.169 --> 00:26:06.659
Well, now we know why
nobody ever saw her again.

00:26:06.659 --> 00:26:08.548
She didn't want to live without him.

00:26:14.479 --> 00:26:15.589
Dean, give me a hand.

00:26:18.089 --> 00:26:18.949
Really?

00:26:21.929 --> 00:26:22.929
What are you gonna do?

00:26:25.659 --> 00:26:27.149
We can't leave her like this.

00:26:27.149 --> 00:26:28.269
Why not?

00:26:28.499 --> 00:26:30.409
She deserves to be put to rest, Dean.

00:26:41.909 --> 00:26:42.759
So...

00:26:47.559 --> 00:26:50.639
So, if you manage to put
Greeley to rest, too...

00:26:51.949 --> 00:26:53.349
What happens to them?

00:26:55.069 --> 00:26:57.528
Lady, that answer is
way beyond our pay grade.

00:26:57.729 --> 00:27:00.349
You hunt these things, but you
don't know what happens to them?

00:27:00.719 --> 00:27:01.869
Well, they never come back.

00:27:01.869 --> 00:27:03.339
That's all that matters.

00:27:06.509 --> 00:27:09.239
After they let go of
whatever'skeeping them here, they...

00:27:10.359 --> 00:27:11.399
They just go.

00:27:12.479 --> 00:27:15.009
I hope someplace better,
but we don't know.

00:27:16.548 --> 00:27:17.819
No one does.

00:27:17.889 --> 00:27:19.739
What happens when you burn their bones?

00:27:20.609 --> 00:27:25.959
Well, my dad used to say that was
like death for ghosts, you know?

00:27:26.259 --> 00:27:27.379
But...

00:27:27.759 --> 00:27:29.709
The truth is, we still don't know.

00:27:30.399 --> 00:27:31.849
Not for sure.

00:27:35.849 --> 00:27:38.709
Guess that's why we all
hold on to life so hard.

00:27:40.249 --> 00:27:41.479
Even the dead.

00:27:43.099 --> 00:27:44.999
We're all just scared of the unknown.

00:27:45.999 --> 00:27:48.179
The only thing I'm
scared of is losing David.

00:27:50.528 --> 00:27:52.028
I have to see him again.

00:28:03.679 --> 00:28:05.269
I have to.

00:28:32.019 --> 00:28:33.729
I think we should tell
her about her husband.

00:28:33.899 --> 00:28:34.788
We can't.

00:28:37.038 --> 00:28:40.419
Dean, it's cruel, letting
her pine for him like this.

00:28:40.419 --> 00:28:41.899
I don't like keeping her in the dark.

00:28:41.899 --> 00:28:43.159
It's for her own good.

00:28:49.109 --> 00:28:51.869
I know you feel guilty,
butlet's just stick to the plan.

00:28:52.069 --> 00:28:52.859
Let's get her out of here.

00:28:52.859 --> 00:28:53.709
Then we'll tell her.

00:28:53.709 --> 00:28:54.869
Tell me what?

00:28:57.298 --> 00:28:58.999
What aren't you telling me?

00:29:02.319 --> 00:29:03.028
It's about David.

00:29:03.028 --> 00:29:04.689
You know what happened to him.

00:29:05.229 --> 00:29:06.669
Molly Sam, don't.

00:29:06.689 --> 00:29:07.829
Don't what?

00:29:09.019 --> 00:29:11.639
Don't tell me because
I'll mess up your hunt?

00:29:11.699 --> 00:29:14.469
You don't care about me or my husband.

00:29:14.469 --> 00:29:15.798
That's not true.

00:29:15.798 --> 00:29:16.869
Really?

00:29:18.559 --> 00:29:20.919
Then whatever it is, tell me, please.

00:29:29.689 --> 00:29:30.709
He's coming.

00:29:32.469 --> 00:29:33.429
Stay with her...

00:30:41.629 --> 00:30:42.709
He's got Molly!

00:31:08.379 --> 00:31:09.649
This guy is persistent.

00:31:09.839 --> 00:31:10.879
We got to find Molly.

00:31:11.028 --> 00:31:12.359
We got to find Greeley's bones.

00:31:12.359 --> 00:31:16.979
And, uh, no pressure or anything, but we
got less than two hours before sunrise.

00:31:18.469 --> 00:31:19.369
Hey.

00:31:20.528 --> 00:31:21.439
What do you got?

00:31:23.159 --> 00:31:25.139
"February 6, 1992. "

00:31:25.659 --> 00:31:27.469
That was like two weeks
before the accident, wasn't it?

00:31:27.469 --> 00:31:28.288
Yeah.

00:31:28.288 --> 00:31:30.239
It looks like the hunting cabin, but...

00:31:30.788 --> 00:31:33.869
I swear there's a tree there
right where they're standing.

00:31:37.649 --> 00:31:38.769
Should have thought of it.

00:31:38.769 --> 00:31:39.879
What?

00:31:39.879 --> 00:31:41.259
It's an old country custom, Dean.

00:31:41.259 --> 00:31:43.399
Planting a tree as a grave marker.

00:31:45.079 --> 00:31:48.009
You're like a walking
encyclopedia of weirdness.

00:31:50.349 --> 00:31:51.059
Yeah.

00:31:51.059 --> 00:31:52.209
I know.

00:31:53.989 --> 00:31:55.199
Where's David?

00:31:56.229 --> 00:31:57.409
What did you do to him?

00:31:59.259 --> 00:32:01.619
You shouldn't worry about him anymore.

00:32:02.489 --> 00:32:03.749
Oh, my god.

00:32:03.919 --> 00:32:06.288
You should worry about yourself.

00:32:07.309 --> 00:32:08.849
I didn't do anything to you.

00:32:08.989 --> 00:32:10.069
Oh?

00:32:13.169 --> 00:32:15.419
I know... I know about your wife.

00:32:16.189 --> 00:32:18.259
Hurting me won't bring her back.

00:32:20.199 --> 00:32:21.798
My wife is gone.

00:32:24.989 --> 00:32:28.759
All I got left'shurting you.

00:32:37.199 --> 00:32:39.219
P-Please.

00:32:39.219 --> 00:32:40.859
Just let me go.

00:32:41.028 --> 00:32:42.038
Go?

00:32:43.559 --> 00:32:44.729
You're not gonna leave.

00:32:45.649 --> 00:32:48.019
You're never gonna leave.

00:32:58.788 --> 00:32:59.879
Go get Molly.

00:33:13.159 --> 00:33:14.139
Oh, thank god.

00:33:14.929 --> 00:33:16.129
Call me Dean.

00:33:24.089 --> 00:33:25.629
This guy's really pissing me off.

00:34:45.588 --> 00:34:47.469
Oh, baby, it's been a long night.

00:34:53.059 --> 00:34:53.788
All right.

00:34:55.929 --> 00:34:57.409
Let's get you out of here.

00:34:58.119 --> 00:35:02.179
I'm not going anywhere until you
tell me what happened to my husband.

00:35:03.438 --> 00:35:04.278
Molly...

00:35:04.458 --> 00:35:08.759
All this time I've been looking
for him, and you knew that...

00:35:09.858 --> 00:35:11.759
You knew that Greeley
killed him, didn't you?

00:35:15.048 --> 00:35:15.929
He's dead.

00:35:17.628 --> 00:35:18.679
No, Molly.

00:35:20.358 --> 00:35:21.949
David's alive.

00:35:22.378 --> 00:35:23.119
What?

00:35:24.898 --> 00:35:25.938
You're sure?

00:35:27.168 --> 00:35:28.268
I'm sure.

00:35:30.288 --> 00:35:31.079
We'll take you to him.

00:35:31.079 --> 00:35:32.298
Come on.

00:35:52.588 --> 00:35:54.688
He's in that house right there.

00:35:56.728 --> 00:35:57.809
I don't understand.

00:35:59.278 --> 00:36:00.248
You will.

00:36:20.179 --> 00:36:22.119
That's not...

00:36:26.668 --> 00:36:27.788
It can't be.

00:36:36.998 --> 00:36:38.358
What's happening?

00:36:41.168 --> 00:36:42.199
Who is that?

00:36:44.498 --> 00:36:45.958
That's David's wife.

00:36:54.009 --> 00:36:55.489
I'm sorry, Molly.

00:36:57.739 --> 00:37:02.068
15 years ago, you and your husband
it Jonah Greeley with your car.

00:37:05.909 --> 00:37:07.429
What are you saying?

00:37:08.309 --> 00:37:11.369
We're saying there isn't just
one spirit haunting highway 41.

00:37:11.369 --> 00:37:12.679
There are two.

00:37:13.478 --> 00:37:15.538
Jonah Greeley and you.

00:37:15.978 --> 00:37:20.248
For the past 15 years, one night a year
you've been appearing on that highway.

00:37:20.248 --> 00:37:21.998
No. That's not possible.

00:37:22.748 --> 00:37:25.759
It was our anniversary...
February 22nd...

00:37:25.759 --> 00:37:27.259
1992.

00:37:27.259 --> 00:37:28.318
Yes.

00:37:28.318 --> 00:37:30.788
Molly, it's 2007.

00:37:35.338 --> 00:37:36.668
Oh, god.

00:37:36.818 --> 00:37:38.518
All right. Tell me about highway 41.

00:37:38.518 --> 00:37:40.668
12 accidents over 15 years.

00:37:40.668 --> 00:37:43.579
Five of them fatal, all of them
happening on the same night.

00:37:43.579 --> 00:37:45.528
So what are we looking
at... interstate dead zone?

00:37:45.528 --> 00:37:46.739
Phantom hitchhiker? What?

00:37:46.739 --> 00:37:47.679
Not quite.

00:37:48.028 --> 00:37:50.849
Year after year, witnesses said
the same thing made 'em crash

00:37:50.849 --> 00:37:56.228
A woman appearing in the middle of the
road being chased by a man covered in blood.

00:37:56.228 --> 00:37:57.528
Two spooks?

00:38:12.079 --> 00:38:13.599
Now, where is Molly buried?

00:38:14.028 --> 00:38:16.599
She... she wasn't buried anywhere.

00:38:17.418 --> 00:38:18.759
She was cremated.

00:38:21.248 --> 00:38:23.068
So much for burning her bones.

00:38:23.119 --> 00:38:24.998
Yeah, but then what's keeping her here?

00:38:35.028 --> 00:38:36.918
Some spirits only see what they want.

00:38:38.019 --> 00:38:39.378
David?!

00:38:39.849 --> 00:38:40.878
David?

00:38:41.838 --> 00:38:42.568
Stop!

00:38:43.588 --> 00:38:45.028
Stop!

00:38:51.709 --> 00:38:53.229
You have to help me.

00:38:53.499 --> 00:38:55.389
Dean, I don't think
she knows she's dead.

00:38:58.889 --> 00:38:59.608
Please!

00:39:00.128 --> 00:39:00.699
Open up!

00:39:00.699 --> 00:39:01.119
Please!

00:39:01.119 --> 00:39:02.019
Okay. All right, all right.

00:39:02.019 --> 00:39:02.798
Just calm down.

00:39:02.798 --> 00:39:03.889
Tell us what happened.

00:39:03.959 --> 00:39:05.019
What are you gonna tell her?

00:39:05.939 --> 00:39:07.059
The truth.

00:39:07.639 --> 00:39:09.709
She's gonna take off running
in the other direction.

00:39:10.829 --> 00:39:12.709
Some spirits hold on too tight.

00:39:14.119 --> 00:39:15.329
Can't let go.

00:39:20.818 --> 00:39:21.829
And Greeley?

00:39:21.979 --> 00:39:26.989
Each year he punishes somebody
for his death... chasing them.

00:39:28.318 --> 00:39:29.838
Torturing them.

00:39:32.329 --> 00:39:36.378
And each year, that somebody is you.

00:39:36.639 --> 00:39:38.509
But I don't remember any of it.

00:39:38.668 --> 00:39:40.639
Because you couldn't
see the truth, Molly.

00:39:44.108 --> 00:39:48.528
So that's why he won't
let me off the highway.

00:39:50.809 --> 00:39:51.778
Because...

00:39:53.019 --> 00:39:54.548
I killed him.

00:39:56.939 --> 00:39:58.648
I killed us both.

00:40:05.869 --> 00:40:08.358
Why didn't you tell me
when you first saw me?

00:40:09.119 --> 00:40:10.689
Why wait until now?

00:40:11.099 --> 00:40:12.409
You wouldn't have believed us.

00:40:13.818 --> 00:40:15.298
And you needed me for bait.

00:40:18.019 --> 00:40:19.439
Well, we needed you.

00:40:22.989 --> 00:40:24.059
David.

00:40:24.318 --> 00:40:26.838
Molly, we brought you
here so you could move on.

00:40:27.809 --> 00:40:29.349
I have to tell him.

00:40:34.039 --> 00:40:34.989
That you love him?

00:40:35.749 --> 00:40:37.209
That you're sorry?

00:40:38.439 --> 00:40:40.439
Molly, he already knows that.

00:40:43.019 --> 00:40:45.559
Look, if you want to go in
there, we're not gonna stop you.

00:40:45.559 --> 00:40:47.889
Yeah, but you are gonna
freak him right out.

00:40:50.318 --> 00:40:51.449
For life.

00:41:02.159 --> 00:41:04.298
David's already said
his good byes, Molly.

00:41:04.918 --> 00:41:06.219
Now it's your turn.

00:41:06.989 --> 00:41:09.608
This is your unfinished business.

00:41:10.798 --> 00:41:12.519
What am I supposed to do?

00:41:15.079 --> 00:41:15.959
Just...

00:41:17.519 --> 00:41:18.389
Let go.

00:41:20.128 --> 00:41:21.128
Of David.

00:41:21.278 --> 00:41:22.689
Of everything.

00:41:23.949 --> 00:41:25.159
You do that...

00:41:26.389 --> 00:41:27.918
We think you'll move on.

00:41:29.309 --> 00:41:31.059
But you don't know where.

00:41:33.358 --> 00:41:34.588
No.

00:41:36.278 --> 00:41:38.179
Molly, you don't belong here.

00:41:39.429 --> 00:41:41.409
Haven't you suffer edlong enough?

00:41:43.989 --> 00:41:45.239
It's time.

00:41:47.099 --> 00:41:48.668
It's time to go.

00:42:38.039 --> 00:42:39.619
I guess she wasn't so bad...

00:42:40.358 --> 00:42:41.469
For a ghost.

00:42:44.349 --> 00:42:46.239
You think she's really
going to a better place?

00:42:47.898 --> 00:42:49.059
I hope so.

00:42:51.189 --> 00:42:52.338
I guess we'll never know.

00:42:52.338 --> 00:42:54.499
Not until we take the
plunge ourselves, huh?

00:42:55.619 --> 00:42:56.878
Doesn't really matter, Dean.

00:42:59.148 --> 00:43:00.878
Hope's kind of the whole point.

00:43:04.249 --> 00:43:05.528
All right, Haley Joel.

00:43:07.168 --> 00:43:08.489
Let's hit the road.



00:04:34.929 --> 00:04:36.429
